<para id="RM00000211100FX" category="C" type-id="3008O" name-id="065A1-00" from="200612">
<dtccode>P0335/13</dtccode>
<dtcname>Crankshaft Position Sensor Circuit</dtcname>
<dtccode>P0339/13</dtccode>
<dtcname>Crankshaft Position Sensor Ne Momentary Interruption</dtcname>
<subpara id="RM00000211100FX_01" type-id="31" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___00002Q100000">
<name>Circuit Description</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<list1 type="nonmark">
<item>
<ptxt>The crankshaft position sensor system consists of the crank angle sensor plate and pickup coil. The crank angle sensor plate has 34 teeth with 2 teeth missing for top dead center detection, and is installed to the crankshaft. The NE signal sensor outputs 34 signals for every 1 engine revolutions. The engine control computer performs cylinder identification based on the G2 signal, and detects the crankshaft angle and engine speed using the NE signal.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
<table frame="all" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
<tgroup cols="3" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
<colspec colnum="01" colname="C01" colwidth="0.9685897     in"/>
<colspec colnum="02" colname="C02" colwidth="3.134191     in"/>
<colspec colnum="03" colname="C03" colwidth="3.044139     in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry colname="C01" valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>DTCNo.</ptxt>
<ptxt>SAE/TCCS</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname="C02" valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>DTC Detection Condition</ptxt>
<ptxt>1. Detection condition 2. Malfunction status 3. Malfunction duration 4. Other</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname="C03" valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Inspection Area</ptxt>
</entry>
