</subpara>
<subpara id="RM00000211100FX_02" type-id="32" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___00002Q200000">
<name>Wiring Diagram</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A130194J03" width="7.106578999in" height="4.7836529in"/>
</figure>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM00000211100FX_03" type-id="51" category="05" proc-id="RM0550J___00002Q300000">
<name>Inspection Procedure</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<atten4>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Using SST (TaSCAN), read the freeze frame data. The freeze frame data records part of the engine operating condition when the malfunction occurred, and this information is useful when troubleshooting.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>First troubleshoot DTCs P0335/13 and P0339/13; if no malfunctioning part is found, a malfunction in the mechanical system is suspected.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten4>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM00000211100FX_04" type-id="01" category="01">
<name>Procedure</name>
<testgrp id="RM00000211100FX_04_0001" proc-id="RM0550J___00002Q400000">
<scantool type="4"/>
<testtitle>Read TaSCAN Data (Engine Speed)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09991-70200</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Connect SST (TaSCAN) to DLC3.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Turn the ignition switch ON and, following the screen display of SST (TaSCAN), select [ECU Data Monitor] - [Engine Speed].</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Start the engine.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Read the [Engine Speed] value while the engine is running.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Specified Condition</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt>A value corresponding to the engine speed is output without interruption</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
<atten4>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Check the engine speed using the line graph display.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>If the engine cannot be started, check the engine speed during cranking.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>If the engine speed is 0, an open or short in the crankshaft position sensor circuit is suspected.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten4>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM00000211100FX_04_0007" fin="true">OK</down>
<right ref="RM00000211100FX_04_0002" fin="false">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM00000211100FX_04_0002" proc-id="RM0550J___00002Q500000">
<testtitle>Inspect Crankshaft Position Sensor</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09082-00030</s-number>
</sstitem>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09083-00170</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using SST (Toyota electrical tester), measure the resistance between the connector terminals.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A064984J15" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<spec>
<title>Resistance</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="3" align="center">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.38in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.38in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="1.37in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Tester Connection</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>1 - 2</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>1150 to 1450Ω</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM00000211100FX_04_0003" fin="false">OK</down>
<right ref="RM00000211100FX_04_0008" fin="true">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM00000211100FX_04_0003" proc-id="RM0550J___00002Q600000">
<testtitle>Inspect Wire Harness and Connector (Engine Control Computer - Crankshaft Position Sensor)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<atten4>
<ptxt>For the wire harness and connector inspection procedure and precautions, see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM0000005D701ZX"/></ptxt>
</atten4>
